{"language":"FCL-1","records":[{"id":"r1","type":"claim","text":"The selected account frames the trouble as specification ambiguity under shifting schedules and proposes tightened, written criteria as the main remedy.","scope":"Reading of the supplied body e3647350a300c0ed.","mentions":["e3647350a300c0ed#BODY"]},{"id":"r2","type":"claim","text":"An alternative reading is that the recurring disputes are negotiations about what kind of household the flat is: a unit with mutual obligations, or three private lives sharing fixtures.","scope":"Conjecture; not derivable from supplied material."},{"id":"r3","type":"claim","text":"Under the alternative reading, writing down done-ness criteria is itself one side of a contested question, enacted without settling it, rather than a neutral clarification.","depends":["r2"]},{"id":"r4","type":"claim","text":"The avoidance of conversations can be a response to the form of the negotiation, including being asked to accept a specified obligation, rather than to the vagueness of prior agreements.","depends":["r2"]},{"id":"r5","type":"problem","text":"Nothing in the supplied material identifies what the flatmates take the household to be, so neither reading can be confirmed from what is available.","scope":"Diagnostic uncertainty."},{"id":"r6","type":"use","text":"Ask the two flatmates separately what they take the flat to be, rather than starting with a shared specification document.","action":"Separate, content-permitting conversations about whether the flat carries mutual obligations or is three overlapping private lives.","consequence":"Surfaces the axis the selected account does not address, at the cost of delaying practical relief on recurring chores.","depends":["r2"]},{"id":"r7","type":"use","text":"Use reaction to the proposal itself, not only to its content, as a distinguishing observation.","action":"Notice whether the withdrawing flatmate engages with the proposed criteria or pulls back from the idea of a written arrangement.","consequence":"Content-engagement supports the ambiguity reading; pullback from the idea supports the unit-versus-privacy reading.","depends":["r2","r4"]},{"id":"r8","type":"use","text":"Consider truce-shaped arrangements that reduce exposure rather than optimize fairness.","action":"Owned zones, or rotations with a default outcome nobody has to negotiate in the moment.","consequence":"Trades some efficiency for reduced mutual exposure, matching a privacy reading if that reading is correct.","depends":["r2","r3"]},{"id":"r9","type":"objection","text":"The rival reading risks pathologizing any attempt to make expectations explicit, and can be used to shield a flatmate who simply does not want to do their share.","bearing":"Bears on r2, r3, r8, and on the selected account's remedies symmetrically: whichever reading is imposed, the remedy can be experienced by the other side as an unreasonable demand."},{"id":"r10","type":"commitment","text":"If the rival reading receives uptake, the conversations it proposes should be limited to one or two flatmates at a time and should not be framed as a prelude to a household-wide settlement.","scope":"Applies only if r6 is pursued.","action":"Keep the separate conversations separate; do not immediately aggregate them into a group decision.","consequence":"Preserves the chance of hearing a divergent reading that a group setting would suppress.","depends":["r6"]},{"id":"r11","type":"commitment","text":"If truce-shaped arrangements are tried and the withdrawing flatmate still declines to engage, the question shifts from chores to whether the living arrangement itself fits, and that shift should be named rather than deferred.","scope":"Contingent on r8 being tried and failing.","action":"Raise the lease-and-living-arrangement question explicitly.","consequence":"Puts a larger decision on the table without forcing it from a chore dispute.","depends":["r8"]}],"uptake":["r2","r6","r7","r9"]}